// Fresh v2 schema — intentionally decoupled from v1's
// compiler/codegen/cel_abi.proto.  Rationale: v2's host surface
// (cel::Compiler / cel::Engine / cel::Instance) doesn't depend on
// v1 types.
//
// Design decisions:
//   - Field numbers are dense and locked.  Extending a message is
//     additive only — never renumber.
//   - `CelType` is recursive and carries enough information for the
//     host marshal to pick the right `Value → CelValue` encoder.
//     Derivable facts (like the internal `Repr` enum) stay derived
//     at decode time; wire payload is minimal.
//   - MAP / LIST in `CelType` are first-class declared variable
//     types — the checker accepts them and codegen routes through
//     the kHost dispatch arm (see `rewrite/map-list-dispatch.md`).
//   - No `cel.expr.CheckedExpr` on the wire.  v1 embedded the full
//     checked AST for host-side re-analysis; v2's host doesn't run
//     a second pass, so the AST stays compile-time-only.
//
// Consumed by compiler_v2/api/internal/abi_decode.{h,cc}.
// Produced by compiler_v2/compile.cc.

